{"theorems":[{"slogan_id":10129013,"theorem_id":25306126,"name":"Corollary 9","body":"A random walk on an undirected graph that is finite, connected and non-bipartite is ergodic.","slogan":"A random walk on a finite, connected, and non-bipartite undirected graph is ergodic. This means the walk converges to a unique stationary distribution regardless of the starting point. The process is both irreducible and aperiodic. It ensures that all states are positive recurrent.","theorem_type":"corollary","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"1202.5569v1","source":"arXiv","title":"The Cover Time of Random Walks on Graphs","authors":["Mohammed Abdullah"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1202.5569v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.PR","categories":["math.PR","cs.DM"],"citations":0,"year":2012,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.7465686202049255,"score":0.7465686202049255,"has_metadata":true},{"slogan_id":7398006,"theorem_id":22481653,"name":"Theorem A.2 (Ergodic Theorem for Markov chains)","body":"Let $(X_0,X_1,$ $X_2,...)$ be an irreducible aperiodic Markov chain with state space $\\mathcal{S}=\\{ s_1,...,s_k\\} $, transition matrix $P$ and arbitrary initial distribution $\\mu ^{(0)}$. Then there exists a unique distribution $\\pi $ which is stationary for the transition matrix $P$. If $\\mu ^{(n)}$ denotes the distribution of $X_n$ then\\begin{equation*}  \\mu ^{(n)} \\xrightarrow {TV} \\pi . \\end{equation*}","slogan":"An irreducible aperiodic Markov chain with a finite state space has a unique stationary distribution. The distribution of the chain converges to this stationary distribution over time. The convergence occurs in total variation. This holds regardless of the initial distribution.","theorem_type":"theorem","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"1206.4162v1","source":"arXiv","title":"Mixing times for the Swapping Algorithm on the Blume-Emery-Griffiths Model","authors":["M. Ebbers","H. Knöpfel","M. Löwe","F. Vermet"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.4162v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.PR","categories":["math.PR"],"citations":0,"year":2012,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.7198195529414494,"score":0.7198195529414494,"has_metadata":true}]}